#
# Halloo, voice and video calls: layer 28 of the matrix. Place, answer and
# end calls through zxvd's call group (call.start, call.accept,
# call.hangup, call.status, call.signal), and keep a history of them.
# zxvd does signalling only: media (capture, codecs, RTP) is the host's
# job and is not wired (H5), so a connected call carries no sound yet.
# The screen always says that Halloo cannot reach emergency services
# (halloo_model.h HALLOO_NO_EMERGENCY). call.signal's messages are not
# encrypted by zxvd, so the model relays them only when the caller says
# the carrier is an encrypted session (halloo_model.h HM4).
#
# One later layer (Kindred, 44) leans on this one, and its layer leans on
# no other, so the general rules here are owned here (CONCEPTS.tsv): the
# minutes of quiet hours left, whether a call may ring now, and a length
# as hours, minutes and seconds. Nothing nearer the core fits: the shared
# blocks are capacities, shares, days and gcds, and almanac.hours is the
# hours past a whole day, not a length's hours. Stillwater (144) owns a
# minute inside a daily window as a truth, but it is built after this
# layer, so it is not used (app_gate.py refuses a use that points
# outward); quiet_left answers how long the quiet lasts, which a ringing
# rule needs and quiet_now does not say.
#
# Witness pairs are of one kind (zxapp.c run_one B3). Eve answers truths
# only and checks each field against its own range alone, so the task's
# "known contact, not blocked, quiet hours as minutes of day" in Eve and
# KRON is split: the quiet hours, a relation across three minutes, are
# KRON and Rust (quiet_left, a number); the ring rule takes quiet_left's
# answer as a field and is Eve and KRON (ring_ok). The model's C
# (halloo_rules.h) is the third witness of each.
#
# zxvd ends ringing at 30 s (call_session.c ring_ms) and has no method to
# change it; the owner's ring time (ring_wait_ok) may be shorter, never
# longer, so the limit is 5000..30000 ms. Defaults taken: no quiet hours
# until the owner sets them, a ring time of 30000 ms.
#
# Planned languages: Gleam (messaging, types) on ring_ok, whether a call
# message may ring. Python already has a runtime (no pending line).
# LabVIEW (dataflow, signal) owns instrument signals; Halloo's signal path
# is media, which zxvd does not wire, so no entry fits it.
zxapp 1
id     halloo
name   Halloo
version 1.0.0
slot   28
layer  L1
matrix 28
icon   icons/l1/028-halloo.svg
budget 233
needs  peers
needs  mic
needs  camera
needs  notify
model  apps/halloo_model.c

# Minutes of quiet hours left at a minute of the day (HR1): 1..1440
# inside them, 0 outside. Rust traps on a minute outside 0..1439, KRON
# answers it: held.
provides quiet_left num opens closes now
logic    kron quiet_left apps/blocks/halloo/quiet.kron
logic    wasm quiet_left apps/blocks/halloo/quiet.wasm

# May this call ring now (HR2): known, not blocked, no quiet hours left.
# Eve declares each flag's one value, KRON reads above 0 as yes: a flag
# that is no flag is held.
provides ring_ok truth known blocked quiet
logic    eve  ring_ok apps/blocks/halloo/ring.eve
logic    kron ring_ok apps/blocks/halloo/ring.kron
pending  Gleam ring_ok

# How long a call may ring (HR3), a limit in Eve; the model's C checks it
# again before keeping the owner's setting.
provides ring_wait_ok truth ringms
logic    eve ring_wait_ok apps/blocks/halloo/wait.eve

# A call's length as h * 10000 + m * 100 + s (HR4): Sutra holds 9(10) ms,
# KRON answers any: held past it or below 0.
provides hms num ms
logic    kron  hms apps/blocks/halloo/hms.kron
logic    sutra hms apps/blocks/halloo/hms.sutra

# A call fits its history record (HR5): MYRA holds the digits, Eve the
# ranges; a direction, media or reason MYRA fits but Halloo does not know
# is held.
provides call_ok truth seq peer dir media reason ms stamp
logic    myra call_ok apps/blocks/halloo/call.myra
logic    eve  call_ok apps/blocks/halloo/call.eve

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check quiet_left opens=1320,1320,1320,1320,420,600,0,0 closes=420,420,420,420,1320,600,1,0 now=1320,1400,419,420,900,600,1,1439 = 540,460,1,0,420,1440,0,1
check quiet_left opens=1320,1320 closes=420,420 now=0,-1 = both
check quiet_left opens=1320,1440 closes=420,420 now=0,0 = both
check ring_ok known=1,0,1,1,1,1 blocked=0,0,1,0,0,1 quiet=0,0,0,1,1440,0 = true,false,false,false,false,false
check ring_ok known=1,2 blocked=0,0 quiet=0,0 = both
check ring_ok known=1,1 blocked=0,0 quiet=0,-1 = both
check ring_wait_ok ringms=5000,30000,4999,30001,0,-1 = true,true,false,false,false,false
check hms ms=0,999,1000,3723000,86399999,9999999999 = 0,0,1,10203,235959,27774639
check hms ms=1000,10000000000 = both
check hms ms=1000,-1 = both
check call_ok seq=1,999999999,1000000000,1,1 peer=1,4294967295,1,10000000000,1 dir=0,1,0,0,0 media=0,1,0,0,0 reason=0,10,0,0,0 ms=0,9999999999,0,0,0 stamp=0,9999999999999,0,0,10000000000000 = true,true,false,false,false
check call_ok seq=1,1 peer=7,7 dir=1,2 media=0,0 reason=1,1 ms=60000,60000 stamp=1700000000000,1700000000000 = both
